{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0027", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$a, b : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$e : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$(a, b)$", "MATH_0007": "$a \\circ e = b \\circ e$", "MATH_0008": "$(Z, e)$", "MATH_0009": "$t : W \\to X$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$a \\circ t = b \\circ t$", "MATH_0012": "$s : W \\to Z$", "MATH_0013": "$t = e \\circ s$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-equalizers}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3fce4695d6de0b67cdb4cde2bbecb565fcbc390def13b6fcf007707c7cbda3c0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c8d549d490bf99424bf0fc16e6349edf9f669f9242a281bea65f1fd511bf4a9", "source_text": "Suppose that <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> are objects of a category <MATH_0003>\nand that <MATH_0004> are morphisms. We say a morphism\n<MATH_0005> is an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>equalizer<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> for the pair <MATH_0006> if\n<MATH_0007> and if <MATH_0008> satisfies the following\nuniversal property: For every morphism <MATH_0009>\nin <MATH_0010> such that <MATH_0011> there exists\na unique morphism <MATH_0012> such that <MATH_0013>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f5a46dc6c92c65325a771ea49b0deb4b75940b7837c47e7a4d8dfc2381d23419", "unit_id": "tag:0028:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0027", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b15315ec3c2fa7b154c0d17c24b63d47f12b572ea3fa602a460510e1a685b882", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c4689188ecb91d5a8c92d75c3042b437374ef21ae2b2a722c6f1df4f13a99563", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nAs in the case of the fibre products above, equalizers when\nthey exist are unique up to unique isomorphism. There is a\nstraightforward generalization of this definition to the\ncase where we have more than <MATH_0001> morphisms.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8a228b3ae22602bf3f93a61a58d9ebc41bf2f004c9958ca4dd529dc6226574b0", "unit_id": "tag:0027:paragraph-0001"}
